 35CL    35CL(P,P'G)                   1969DU08,1970TA02,1972BR45ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 19-Aug-2025)          
 35CL c  Also include (p,p') measurements listed below.                         
 35CL c  {+35}Cl(p,p'|g) measurements:                                          
 35CL c  1969Du08: E=4.6-6.2 MeV 0.05 |mA proton beam. Thin targets of CdCl{-2} 
 35CL2c  (99% {+35}Cl), 100 |mg/cm{+2}. A 300 |mm annular surface-barrier       
 35CL3c  detector on the beam axis and a movable 390 |mm surface-barrier        
 35CL4c  detector rotated from 20|' to 148|' relative to beam direction for     
 35CL5c  detecting protons, FWHM=24 keV; a 7.62 by 7.62-cm-diam NaI(Tl) crystal 
 35CL6c  and 15- and 35-cc Ge(Li) for detecting |g-rays. Measured |s(E{-p},|q), 
 35CL7c  E|g, I|g, p|g(|q). Deduced levels, J|p, branchings, mixing ratios,     
 35CL8c  half-lives using Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM).              
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1970Ta02: E=4.24, 4.82, 5.08 and 5.11 MeV proton beams produced from   
 35CL2c  the Universite Montreal EN tandem accelerator. Targets of 16 |mg/cm{+2}
 35CL3c  AgCl evaporated onto 0.013 cm gold foils, 99% enriched in {+35}Cl. A   
 35CL4c  12.70-cm-diam by 15.24-cm-long NaI(Tl) and a 30 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector 
 35CL5c  for detecting |g-rays. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q), |g(lin pol). Deduced 
 35CL6c  levels, J|p, branchings, mixing ratios.                                
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Br45: E=3.45-6.00 MeV protons produced from the University of      
 35CL2c  Auckland folded tandem accelerator. Natural chlorine targets of AgCl,  
 35CL3c  PbCl{-2} and solid Cl (75.77% {+35}Cl, 24.33% {+37}Cl). A 25 cm{+3}    
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector for detecting |g-rays, FWHM=2.3 keV for E|g=1.332 MeV. 
 35CL5c  Measured E|g. Deduced levels, half-lives using DSAM. 1972Br45 report a 
 35CL6c  few mixing ratios in their TABLE V, but it is unclear where they are   
 35CL7c  taken from. They are definitely not from 1972Br45 since this work is   
 35CL8c  only focused on lifetime measurements                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Va06: E=5.47-5.61 MeV protons from the 5.5 MV Van de Graaff        
 35CL2c  accelerator of the Southern Universities Nuclear Institute. Targets of 
 35CL3c  BaCl{-2} (99% {+35}Cl) on gold backings. A 57 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector.  
 35CL4c  Measured E|g. Deduced half-lives using DSAM.                           
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1961St09: E=2.3-3.25 MeV. NaI(Tl) detector. Targets of AgCl. Measured  
 35CL2c  |s(E{-p},|q), |g(|q). Deduced levels, J for the levels of 1.22 and 1.76
 35CL3c  MeV.                                                                   
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1966Er06: E=0.733-2.595 MeV protons produced from the Utrecht 3 MV Van 
 35CL2c  de Graaff accelerator. BaCl{-2} target (99.5% {+35}Cl) on a tantalum   
 35CL3c  backing. Cylindrical NaI assemblies, 10-cm by 10-cm. Measured E|g,     
 35CL4c  |g(|q). Deduced levels, J|p, mixing ratios, mainly for {+36}Ar and for 
 35CL5c  the {+35}Cl level at E{-x}=1760.                                       
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1970Ta09: E=5.11 MeV proton beam. NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g.      
 35CL2c  Developed an analytical method to interpret the linear polarization    
 35CL3c  measurement of two unresolved |g-rays: 3.00 and 3.16 MeV. Same authors 
 35CL4c  as 1970Ta02                                                            
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1971Ca40: E=4.15-6.15 MeV protons from the Oxford University Tandem    
 35CL2c  accelerator. Targets of 20 |mg/cm{+2} natural BaCl{-2} on gold, lead,  
 35CL3c  and carbon backings. A 32 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g. Deduced
 35CL4c  half-lives for the levels of 2646 and 2695 keV using DSAM.             
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1974Hu09: E=5.65 MeV protons from the pulsed beam facility of the      
 35CL2c  University of Alberta Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets of natural KCl
 35CL3c  on tantalum backing and PbCl{-2} on gold backing. A 24 cm{+3} coaxial  
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g. Deduced half-life for the level of 3162 
 35CL5c  keV.                                                                   
 35CL c  Other (p,p'|g) measurement: 1985Ki07 and 1975De16 (measured 1219|g     
 35CL2c  yield)                                                                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  (p,p') measurements:                                                   
 35CL c  1969Ta13,1971Ta02: E=3.115 and 3.345 MeV protons produced from the     
 35CL2c  Universite de Montreal Model EN tandem accelerator. AgCl target (99%   
 35CL3c  {+35}Cl) of 16 |mg/cm{+2} on gold backing. A 12.70-cm-diam by          
 35CL4c  15.24-cm-long NaI(Tl) for detecting |g-rays. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q).
 35CL5c  Deduced levels, J|p and mixing ratio for the level of 1763 keV. Same   
 35CL6c  authors as 1970Ta02                                                    
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1969An35: E=6.03 MeV proton beams on a CdCl{-2} target. Inelastic      
 35CL2c  protons detected by a Si(Li) detector. Measured |s(E{-p'},|q). Deduced 
 35CL3c  J for a level at 3930.                                                 
 35CL c  Other (p,p') measurement: 1993Bo40 (measured |s)                       
 35CL cG E$E|g values with uncertainties for the ground-state transitions are   
 35CL2cG not explicitly listed in 1972Br45 and 1969Du08 and the evaluators have 
 35CL3cG taken their listed E(level) values and uncertainties (which are deduced
 35CL4cG from E|g values by authors) as E|g values of the corresponding         
 35CL5cG ground-state transitions, considering ground-state transitions are     
 35CL6cG dominant in each level.                                                
 35CL cG RI$Relative photon branching ratios deduced by the evaluators based on 
 35CL2cG percentage branching ratios reported in 1970Ta02 and 1969Du08, which   
 35CL3cG are given under comments where available.                              
 35CL cG M,MR$From |g(|q) and |g(lin pol) in 1970Ta02, unless otherwise noted.  
 35CL cG E(A)$From 1969Du08                                                     
 35CL cG E(C),RI(C)$|g reported in 1970Ta02. Energy is from level-energy        
 35CL2cG difference and intensity is from 1970Ta02. The ones with I|g reported  
 35CL3cG as upper limit are considered questionable by the evaluators.          
 35CL cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies with uncertainties,      
 35CL2cL unless otherwise noted.                                                
 35CL cL J$From Adopted Levels. Supporting arguments from this dataset are given
 35CL2cL under comments if available.                                           
